&Q000381 = The lament for Nibru
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.2.4
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.2.4&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div kirugu A

A.1. tur₃ me nun-e ba-du₃-a-bi
#tr.en: After the cattle pen had been built for the foremost divine powers -- how did it become a haunted place?
#lem: tur[animal stall]; me[Being]; nun[prince]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 33; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 27

A.2. lil₂-e a-gin₇ ib₂-sag₃ ki-bi me-na gi₄-gi₄
#tr.en: When will it be restored?
#lem: lil[ghost]; agin[thus]; sag[strike]; ki[place]; mena[when?]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. %e še-eb na-aŋ₂-tar-ra ba-mar-ra %s re
#tr.en: Where once the brick of fate had been laid -- who scattered its divine powers?
#lem: šeb[brick]N; naŋtar[fate]N; mar[place]V/t; re[that]
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. me-bi a-ba-a in-bir-re %e a-še-er %s ba-da-tab
#tr.en: The lamentation is reprised: how did the storeroom of @wSN{Nibru},
#lem: me[Being]; aba[who?]; bir[scatter]; ašer[lament]N; tab[double]
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. šudum nibru{ki} eš₃ dur-an-ki-a
#tr.en: the shrine @wTN{Dur-an-ki}, become a haunted place? When will it be restored?
#lem: šutum[storehouse]; Nibru[1]SN; eš[shrine]; Durankik[1]TN
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. lil₂-e a-gin₇ ib₂-sag₃ ki-bi me-na gi₄-gi₄
#tr.en: After @wTN{Ki-ur}, the great place,
#lem: lil[ghost]; agin[thus]; sag[strike]; ki[place]; mena[when?]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. ki-ur₃ ki gal ba-du₃-a-bi
#tr.en: had been built,
#lem: Kiʾur[1]; ki[place]; gal[big]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. %e še-eb %s e₂-kur-ra ba-du₃-a-bi
#tr.en: after the brickwork of @wTN{E-kur} had been built,
#lem: šeb[brick]N; Ekur[1]TN; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. ub-šu-unken-na ba-du₃-a-bi
#tr.en: after @wTN{Ubšu-unkena} had been built,
#lem: Ubšuʾunkenak[1]TN; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. eš₃ e₂-gal-mah ba-du₃-a-bi
#tr.en: after the shrine @wTN{Egal-maḫ} had been built -- how did they become haunted?
#lem: eš[shrine]; Egalmah[1]TN; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. lil₂-e a-gin₇ ib₂-sag₃ ki-bi me-na gi₄-gi₄
#tr.en: When will they be restored?
#lem: lil[ghost]; agin[thus]; sag[strike]; ki[place]; mena[when?]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. %e uru₂ %s zid šag₄-sug₄-ga a-gin₇ ba-an-[du₃]
#tr.en: How did the true city become empty?
#lem: uru[city]; zid[right]; šagsug[empty]; agin[thus]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. ŋiš-hur kal-la-bi šu pe-el-la ba-ab#-[dug₄]
#tr.en: Its precious designs have been defiled!
#lem: ŋešhur[plan]; kal[rare]; šu[hand]; pel[defile]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. %e uru₂-a i₃-zi-iŋ₃-bi %s a-gin₇ ba-an-[šub]
#tr.en: How were the city's festivals neglected?
#lem: uru[city]; izeŋ[festival]; agin[thus]; šub[fall]
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. ŋarza mah-bi šu suh₃-a ba-ab-[dug₄]
#tr.en: Its magnificent rites have been thrown into disorder!
#lem: ŋarza[rites]; mah[great]; šu[hand]; suh[confuse]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. nibru#{ki} šag₄-ba me hal-hal-a
#tr.en: In the heart of @wSN{Nibru},
#lem: Nibru[1]SN; šag[heart]; me[Being]; hal[divide]
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. uŋ₃ saŋ gig₂-ga numun zid ib₂-i-i-a
#tr.en: where the divine powers were allotted and the black-headed people prolificly multiplied,
#lem: uŋ[people]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; numun[seed]; zid[right]; e[bring out]
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. %e uru₂ %s šag₄-bi umuš ba-ra-pad₃-da
#tr.en: the city's heart no longer revealed any sign of intelligence -- there where the @wDN{Anuna} used to give advice!
#lem: uru[city]; šag[heart]; umuš[consideration]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. {d}a-nun-na-ke₄-ne na ba-an-degₓ(RI)-ge-eš-am₃
#tr.en: In @wTN{Ubšu-unkena},
#lem: Anunak[1]DN; na[cvne]; deg[gather up]
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. ub-šu-unken-na ki di gal ku₅-ru
#tr.en: the place for making great judgments,
#lem: Ubšuʾunkenak[1]TN; ki[place]; did[lawsuit]; gal[big]; kud[break off]
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. eš-bar-e si sa₂ ba-ra-an-zu-uš-am₃
#tr.en: they no longer impart decisions or justice!
#lem: ešbar[decision]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. diŋir-be₂-ne ki-tuš ba-ab-ŋar-ra
#tr.en: Where its gods had established their dwellings,
#lem: diŋir[deity]; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

A.23. šukur₂-ud-bi im-šub-ba barag-bi im-ri-a
#tr.en: where their daily rations were offered,
#lem: šukurud[daily ration]; šub[fall]; barag[sanctum]; ri[impose]
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

A.24. |KI.LUGAL.GUB| kug kiŋ₂-sig₇ unu₂ gal-ba
#tr.en: their daises erected,
#lem: KI.LUGAL.DU[cultic place]; kug[purify]; kiŋsig[afternoon meal]; unu[dwelling]; gal[big]
#etcsl: line-id=A.24

A.25. kurun₂ lal₃ bal-bal-e nam-še₃ bi₂-ib₂-tar-ra
#tr.en: where the sacred royal offering (?) and the evening meal in their great banquet hall were destined for the pouring out of choice beer and syrup -- @wSN{Nibru},
#lem: kurun[beer]; lal[syrup]; bala[turn]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=A.25

A.26. nibru{ki} %e uru₂ %s ŋissu daŋal-la-bi-še₃
#tr.en: the city where the black-headed people used to cool themselves in its spreading shade -- in their dwellings @wDN{Enlil} fell upon them as if they were criminals.
#lem: Nibru[1]SN; uru[city]; ŋissu[shade]; daŋal[wide]
#etcsl: line-id=A.26

A.27. uŋ₃ saŋ gig₂-ga ni₂ im-ši-ib₂-te-en-na
#tr.en: It was he who sent them scattering,
#lem: uŋ[people]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; ni[self]; ten[extinguish]
#etcsl: line-id=A.27

A.28. ki-tuš-ba gu₂-zal-a-gin₇ ba-ra-an-šub
#tr.en: like a scattered herd of cattle.
#lem: kituš[dwelling place]; guzal[scoundrel]; šub[fall]
#etcsl: line-id=A.28

A.29. ab₂ sag₂ dug₄-ga-gin₇ e-ne sag₂ ba-ra-an-dug₄
#tr.en: How long until its lady,
#lem: ab[cow]; sag[scatter]; dug[speak]; ane[he]; sag[scatter]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.29

A.30. %e uru₂ %s šag₄-bi er₂ gig dirig-ga
#tr.en: the goddess @wDN{Ninlil},
#lem: uru[city]; šag[heart]; er[tears]; gig[sick]; dirig[make more than]
#etcsl: line-id=A.30

A.31. en-na-me-še₃ diŋir %e ga-ša-an-bi %s en₃-bi nu-tar-re
#tr.en: would ask after the inner city, whose bitter tears were overwhelming?
#lem: ennameše[how long?]; diŋir[deity]; gašan[lady]N; en[cvne]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=A.31

A.32. e₂ gu-la za-pa-aŋ₂ ib₂-zu-a-bi
#tr.en: As though it were empty wasteland,
#lem: e[house]; gal[big]; zipaŋ[voice]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=A.32

A.33. e₂-ri-a sug₄-gin₇ lu₂ nu-un-ku₄-ku₄
#tr.en: no one enters that great temple whose bustle of activity was famous.
#lem: eria[wasteland]; sug[empty]; lu[person]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=A.33

A.34. nibru{ki} iri{ki} barag-barag gal-gal-e-ne šu im-ma-an-peš₁₁-eš-a-aš a-na-aš u₂-gu i₃-ni-in-de₂-eš
#tr.en: As for all the great rulers who increased the wealth of the city of @wSN{Nibru} -- why did they disappear?
#lem: Nibru[1]SN; iri[city]; barag[sanctum]; gal[big]; šu[hand]; peš[thick]; anaš[why?]; ugu[cvne]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=A.34

A.35. (1:uŋ₃:1) saŋ gig₂-ga u₂ hi-a udu-gin₇ bi₂-ib₂-gu₇-a
#tr.en: For how long would @wDN{Enlil} neglect the Land,
#lem: uŋ[people]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; u[plant(s)]; hi[mix (up)]; udu[sheep]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=A.35

:35v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) %e ka-na-aŋ₂
?#tr.en: where the black-headed @varh[t224.v1]{people } @vart[t224.v2,t224.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} Land } @vart[t224.v3,t224.v1]{@varn{another ms. has instead:} city } ate rich grass like sheep?
?#tr.en: Tears, lamentation, depression and despair!
?#tr.en: How long would his spirit burn and his heart not be placated?
?#tr.en: Why were those who once played the @fsux{šem} and @fsux{ala} drums spending their time in bitter lamenting?
?#tr.en: Why were the lamenters sitting in its brick buildings?
?#tr.en: They were bewailing the hardship which beset them.
#lem: kanaŋ[land]
:35v.1.2: ($another ms. has instead:$) %e uru₂
#lem: uru[city]

A.36. ud en-še₃ i₃-šub er₂ a-nir šag₄ sag₃ ur₅ uš₂-a
#lem: ud[sun]; enše[how long]; šub[fall]; er[tears]; anir[lament]; šag[heart]; sag[strike]; ur[liver]; uš[die]
#etcsl: line-id=A.36

A.37. en-še₃ bar bi₂-ib-tab₂ šag₄ nu-ub-ši-huŋ-e
#lem: enše[how long]; bar[outside]; tab[burn]; šag[heart]; huŋ[pacify]
#etcsl: line-id=A.37

A.38. {kuš}šem₅ {kuš}a₂-la₂ mu-un-du₁₂-a re
#lem: šem[drum]; ala[wooden drum]; du[play (a musical instrument)]; re[that]
#etcsl: line-id=A.38

A.39. i-lu gig-ga-a a-na-še₃ ud mi-ni-ib₂-zal
#lem: ilu[lament]; gig[sick]; anaš[why?]; ud[sun]; zal[pass time]
#etcsl: line-id=A.39

A.40. balaŋ di šeg₁₂-ba e-ne ba-dur₂-ru-ne-eš
#lem: balaŋ[an instrument]; di[speak]; šeg[brick]; ana[what?]; durun[sit]
#etcsl: line-id=A.40

A.41. kuš₂-a ŋar-ra-bi er₂-še₃ ba-ab-be₂-ne
#lem: kušu[tired]; ŋar[put]; er[tears]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.41

A.42. lu₂ dam šub-ba dumu šub-ba-ne
#tr.en: The men whose wives had fallen, whose children had fallen,
#lem: lu[person]; dam[spouse]; šub[fall]; dumu[child]; šub[fall]
#etcsl: line-id=A.42

A.43. a %e uru₂ %s hul-a-me šir₃-re-eš ba-ab-be₂-ne
#tr.en: were singing @q[men of Nibru,others]{“Oh our destroyed city!”}. Their city gone,
#lem: aya[cry]; uru[city]; hulu[bad]; šir[song]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.43

A.44. %e uru₂-bi %s e₃-a ki-tuš-bi kar-ra
#tr.en: their homes abandoned -- as those who were singing for the brick buildings of the good city,
#lem: uru[city]; e[leave]; kituš[dwelling place]; kar[flee]
#etcsl: line-id=A.44

A.45. šeg₁₂ %e uru₂ %e ze₂-ba-še₃ %s im-ši-šir₃-šir₃-e-ne-eš
#tr.en: as the lamenters of wailing,
#lem: šeg[brick]; uru[city]; zeb[good]V/i; šir[song]
#etcsl: line-id=A.45

A.46. er₂ dug₄-ga balaŋ di-ne-ne-eš₂
#tr.en: like the foster-children of an ecstatic no longer knowing their own intelligence,
#lem: er[tears]; dug[speak]; balaŋ[an instrument]; di[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.46

A.47. a₂-e₃ lu₂-ed₃-da umuš-bi nu-zu-gin₇
#tr.en: the people were smitten,
#lem: aʾea[foster-child]; luʾede[ecstatic]; umuš[consideration]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=A.47

A.48. [uŋ₃] ba#-sag₃ dim₂-ma-bi ba-suh₃
#tr.en: their minds thrown into disorder.
#lem: uŋ[people]; sag[strike]; dimma[thought]; suh[confuse]
#etcsl: line-id=A.48

A.49. [e₂ zid]-de₃# er₂ gig-ga-bi im-me
#tr.en: The true temple wails bitterly.
#lem: e[house]; zid[right]; er[tears]; gig[sick]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.49

@div trailer 

A.50. ki#-ru-gu₂ 1-a-kam
#tr.en: 1st @fsux{kirugu }
#lem: kirugu[division notation in certain literary compositions]; n
#etcsl: line-id=A.50

@end trailer

@end kirugu

@div ŋišgiŋal B

B.51. [...] X e₂ mu-un-du₃ {d}nin-lil₂ NA
#tr.en: …… built the temple, @wDN{Ninlil} …….
#lem: X; X; e[house]; du[build]; Ninlil[1]DN; X
#etcsl: line-id=B.51

@div trailer 

B.52. ŋiš#-gi₄-ŋal₂-bi-im
#tr.en: Its @fsux{ŋišgiŋal }
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]
#etcsl: line-id=B.52

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div kirugu C

C.53. e₂ zid-de₃ er₂ %e a-še-er %s ma-ra-ba
#tr.en: The true temple gave you only tears and lamentation -- it sings a bitter song of the proper cleansing-rites that are forgotten!
#lem: e[house]; zid[right]; er[tears]; ašer[lament]N; ba[allot]
#etcsl: line-id=C.53

C.54. šir₃ gig-ga im-me šu-luh zid ha-lam-[ma-še₃]
#tr.en: The brickwork of @wTN{E-kur} gave you only tears and lamentation -- it sings a bitter song of the proper cleansing-rites that are forgotten!
#lem: šir[sing]; gig[sick]; dug[speak]; šuluh[ritual cleansing]; zid[right]; halam[forsake]
#etcsl: line-id=C.54

C.55. %e še-eb %s e₂-kur-ra-ke₄ er₂ %e a-še-er %s ma-ra-ba
#tr.en: It weeps bitter tears over the splendid rites and most precious plans which are desecrated -- its most sacred food rations neglected and …… into funeral offerings,
#lem: šeb[brick]N; Ekur[1]TN; er[tears]; ašer[lament]N; ba[allot]
#etcsl: line-id=C.55

C.56. šir₃ gig-ga im-me šu-luh zid ha-[lam-ma]-še₃
#tr.en: it cries @q[E-kur,]{“Alas!”}. The temple despairs of its divine powers,
#lem: šir[sing]; gig[sick]; dug[speak]; šuluh[ritual cleansing]; zid[right]; halam[forsake]
#etcsl: line-id=C.56

C.57. ŋarza mah ŋiš-hur kal-kal šu hul dug₄-ga er₂ gig i₃-še₂₂-še₂₂
#tr.en: utterly cleansed,
#lem: ŋarza[rites]; mah[great]; ŋešhur[plan]; kal[rare]; šu[hand]; hulu[bad]; dug[speak]; er[tears]; gig[sick]; šeš[weep]
#etcsl: line-id=C.57

C.58. šukur₂ šub-šub-ba kug-kug-ga-bi ki-sig₁₀-ga X-ba muš₂-am₃-bi im-me
#tr.en: pure, hallowed, which are now defiled!
#lem: šukur[food allocation]; šub[fall]; kug[pure]; kisiga[funerary offerings]; X; mušam[(exclamation of) compassion]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=C.58

C.59. me luh-luh-ha sikil šen-na-bi šu pel-la₂-ke₄-eš e₂-e ur₅ ib₂-uš₂
#tr.en: The true temple,
#lem: me[Being]; luh[clean]; sikil[purify]; šen[pure]; šu[hand]; pel[defile]; e[house]; ur[liver]; uš[die]
#etcsl: line-id=C.59

C.60. e₂ zid-de₃ ni₂-bi sun₅-sun₅ gig-ga-a
#tr.en: which it is bitter to enter on one's own,
#lem: e[house]; zid[right]; ni[self]; sun[plural stem of kur⟦to enter⟧]; gig[sick]
#etcsl: line-id=C.60

C.61. ud mi-ni-ib₂-zal-zal-e er₂ im-gibil-[gibil]
#tr.en: passes the time renewing its tears.
#lem: ud[sun]; zal[pass time]; er[tears]; gibil[new]
#etcsl: line-id=C.61

C.62. e₂-a niŋ₂ ŋar-ra niŋ₂ dirig-bi kišib-bi ib₂-du₈-a-aš gun₂ ki mu-ni-ib₂-ŋal₂
#tr.en: Because the sealings of the abundant materials stored in the temple have been broken open, they have placed the loads on the ground.
#lem: e[house]; niŋ[thing]; ŋar[put]; niŋ[thing]; dirig[make more than]; kišib[cylinder seal]; du[spread]; gun[load]; ki[place]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=C.62

C.63. niŋ₂-gur₁₁ erim₃ saŋ sig₁₀-ga-ba šu gi₄ ba-ab-dug₄-a-aš a-na ma-la₂ im-me
#tr.en: Because the property in its well-tended storehouses has been sent back, it says @q[E-kur,]{“What will they weigh out for me now?”}; because the enemies who do not know good from evil have cut off all good things,
#lem: niŋgur[property]; erim[storeroom]; saŋ[head]; sig[put into]; šu[hand]; gi[turn]; dug[speak]; ana[what?]; la[hang]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=C.63

C.64. lu₂-kur₂-ra sag₉ hul nu-zu-ne niŋ₂ dug₃ bi₂-ib-ku₅-ru-uš-a-aš i-lu gig im-me
#tr.en: it sings a bitter dirge; because they have finished off its populace there like animals,
#lem: lukur[stranger]; sag[goodness]; hulu[bad]; zu[know]; niŋ[thing]; dug[good]; kud[cut]; ilu[lament]; gig[sick]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=C.64

C.65. nam-lu₂-ulu₃-bi maš₂-anše-gin₇ šag₄-ba mi-ni-ib-til-la-aš a %e ka-na-aŋ₂-ŋu₁₀ %s im-me
#tr.en: it cries @q[E-kur,]{“Oh my Land!”}. Because they have piled up the young women, young men and their little children like heaps of grain,
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; mašanše[animals]; šag[heart]; til[complete]; aya[cry]; kanaŋ[land]N; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=C.65

C.66. ki-sikil ŋuruš di₄-di₄-la₂-be₂-ne zar-re-eš mi-ni-ib-sal-la-aš u₈-a-bi im-me
#tr.en: it cries @q[E-kur,]{“Woe!”} for them.
#lem: kisikil[young woman]; ŋuruš[young adult male]; didila[small(er)]; zar[sheaf (of barley)]; sal[thin]; ua[oh!]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=C.66

C.67. urin-bi muru₉ šeŋ₃-ŋa₂-gin₇ ki-e bi₂-ib-su₃-a-aš er₂-še₃ nu-gul-e
#tr.en: Because they have splashed their blood on the ground like a rain-storm, there is no restraint to its crying.
#lem: urin[blood]; muru[rainstorm]; šeŋ[rain]; ki[place]; su[sprinkle]; er[tears]; gul[destroy]
#etcsl: line-id=C.67

C.68. e₂-e ab₂ amar-bi ku₅-ra₂-gin₇ ni₂-bi-še₃ mur gig-ga im-ša₄ šeₓ(SIG₇)-šeₓ(SIG₇) i₃-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#tr.en: The temple, like a cow whose calf is cut off, groans bitterly to itself;
#lem: e[house]; ab[cow]; amar[calf]; kud[cut]; ni[self]; mur[noise]; gig[sick]; ša[cvve]; še[tear]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=C.68

C.69. balaŋ di lu₂ ad dug₃-ga-ke₄-ne emeda(|UM.ME|){da} u₅-a di-gin₇ mu-bi er₂-ra mi-ni-ib-bal-bal-e-ne
#tr.en: it is grief-stricken, and the sweet-voiced lamenters, like nursemaids singing a lullaby, respond tearfully with its name.
#lem: balaŋ[an instrument]; di[speak]; lu[person]; ad[voice]; dug[good]; emeda[nursemaid]; ua[oh!]; di[speak]; mu[name]; er[tears]; bala[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=C.69

C.70. %e uru₂ %e u₃-mu-un-bi %s saŋ ib₂-ta-an-dub₂-ba-aš
#tr.en: In anguish they bewail the fact that the city's lord has smashed heads there,
#lem: uru[city]; umun[lord]N; saŋ[head]; dub[tremble]
#etcsl: line-id=C.70

C.71. %e i-bi₂-ni %s ki kur₂-ra ib₂-ta-an-ŋar-ra ad-e-eš ba-an-ša₄-aš
#tr.en: that he has looked away from it and toward a foreign land instead.
#lem: ibi[eye]N; ki[place]; kur[different]; ŋar[put]; ad[voice]; ša[cvve]
#etcsl: line-id=C.71

C.72. e₂ zid kur-kur-ra %e i-bi₂-še₃ %s ba-ŋen-na
