@div kirugu E

E.79. %e uru₂ %e u₃-mu-un-bi %s šag₄ ba-da-an-dab-ba
#tr.en: How long will the city's lord who became angry with it not turn to it, not say @q[Enlil,E-kur]{“Alas!”}
#lem: uru[city]; umun[lord]N; šag[heart]; dab[seize]
#etcsl: line-id=E.79

E.80. en-še₃ la-ba-ši-gur-ru muš₃-am₃-bi nu-um-me
#tr.en: for it? Why did he cut off the road to its brickwork? He made the noisy pigeons fly away from their windows.
#lem: enše[how long]; gur[turn]; mušam[(exclamation of) compassion]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=E.80

E.81. šeg₁₂-bi a-na-še₃ ŋiri₃ ib₂-ta-an-ŋar
#tr.en: Why did he transform the appearance of the temple which knew voices,
#lem: šeg[brick]; anaš[why?]; ŋiri[foot]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=E.81

E.82. tum₁₂{mušen} za-pa-aŋ₂ ŋa₂-ŋa₂-bi ab-ta ib₂-ta-an-dal
#tr.en: where they used to while away the days in sweet playing of @fsux{tigi} drums in the brick buildings?
#lem: tum[wild dove]; zipaŋ[voice]; ŋar[put]; ab[window]; dal[fly]
#etcsl: line-id=E.82

E.83. e₂ ad zu šeg₁₂ tigi %e aŋ₂ ze₂-ba %s ud mi-ni-ib-zal-zal-la %e ta-aš %s igi bi₂-in-gi₄
#tr.en: The temple,
#lem: e[house]; ad[voice]; zu[know]; šeg[brick]; tigi[drum or other musical instrument]; aŋ[thing]N; zeb[good]V/i; ud[sun]; zal[pass time]; taš[why?]; igi[eye]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=E.83

E.84. e₂ sun₅-na giri₁₇ šu ŋal₂-la re
#tr.en: once a place to offer salutations in humility,
#lem: e[house]; sun[humble]; kiri[nose]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; re[that]
#etcsl: line-id=E.84

E.85. e₂ ni₂ nu-tuku-gin₇ sig₉-ga-bi ba-du₃
#tr.en: is now as deathly silent as a temple which no one reveres!
#lem: e[house]; ni[fear]; tuku[acquire]; sig[silent]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=E.85

E.86. %e aŋ₂ %s išib-bi nu-kug-kug-ga-gin₇
#tr.en: As though its purification priest's equipment were not utterly sacred,
#lem: aŋ[thing]N; išib[purification priest]; kug[purify]
#etcsl: line-id=E.86

E.87. šu-luh-bi kur-kur-ra nu-ub-ta-sed₆-a-gin₇
#tr.en: as though its cleansing-rites did not bring calm in all countries,
#lem: šuluh[ritual cleansing]; kur[mountain(s)]; sed[cold]
#etcsl: line-id=E.87

E.88. šu bi₂-in-dag gaba-ni ib₂-ta-an-zig₃
#tr.en: he has abandoned it, turned his breast away from it,
#lem: šu[hand]; dag[roam around]; gaba[breast]; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=E.88

E.89. %e aŋ₂-gig %s ur₅-ra-a %e a-še-er-ra %s mu-un-du₃
#tr.en: among dejection and lamentation he has made it a sacrilege.
#lem: aŋgig[bad thing]N; ura[dejection?]; ašer[lament]N; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=E.89

E.90. %e ta-še %s eŋer %e na-aŋ₂-bi i-bi₂-ni-a %s la-ba-an-barag₂
#tr.en: After its fate, how long till his face would be streaked with teardrops?
#lem: taš[why?]; egir[back]; naŋ[fate]N; ibi[eye]N; barag[spread out]
#etcsl: line-id=E.90

E.91. %e aŋ₂ %s sikil du₃-a-gin₇ ur₅-re zag bi₂-in-tag
#tr.en: He rejected it thus as though it were a blasphemy!
#lem: aŋ[thing]N; sikil[purify]; du[build]; ur[that]; zag[side]; tag[touch]
#etcsl: line-id=E.91

E.92. šeg₁₂-bi hul₂-e a-na-aš ib₂-ta-an-e₃
#tr.en: Why has joy left its brickwork?
#lem: šeg[brick]; hul[rejoice]; anaš[why?]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=E.92

E.93. ŋi₆ an-bar₇-ba šag₄-ba er₂ bi₂-in-si
#tr.en: Night and day he has filled its heart with tears!
#lem: ŋi[night]; anbar[mid-day]; šag[heart]; er[tears]; si[fill]
#etcsl: line-id=E.93

E.94. a₂-še kur₂ %e aŋ₂-gig %s bi₂-ib-ak-a
#tr.en: Even now, he has made it foreign and a sacrilege!
#lem: aše[now]; kur[alienate]; aŋgig[bad thing]N; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=E.94

E.95. %e u₃-mu-un-bi %s im-hul-am₃ šu-bi bi₂-in-gi₄-am₃
#tr.en: Its lord, who has despoiled it like an evil wind,
#lem: umun[lord]N; imhul[destructive wind]; šu[hand]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=E.95

E.96. %e uru₂-bi %s e₂-bi in-gul-gul-am₃
#tr.en: has destroyed that city and its temples!
#lem: uru[city]; e[house]; gul[destroy]
#etcsl: line-id=E.96

E.97. ur₂-bi in-bur₁₂-ra-am₃ al-e bi₂-in-ra-am₃
#tr.en: He has ripped out their foundations,
#lem: ur[root]; bur[tear out]; e[speak]; rah[beat]
#etcsl: line-id=E.97

E.98. dam dumu-bi šag₄-ba mi-ni-in-ug₅-ga-am₃
#tr.en: struck them with the adze,
#lem: dam[spouse]; dumu[child]; šag[heart]; ug[kill]
#etcsl: line-id=E.98

E.99. %e uru₂-bi %e uru₂ %s šub-ba im-ma-ni-in-kur₉-ra-am₃
#tr.en: killed wives and their children within it,
#lem: uru[city]; uru[city]; šub[fall]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=E.99

E.100. %e aŋ₂ %s ul-bi ki-bi bi₂-in-[gi₄-am₃]
#tr.en: he has turned that city into a deserted city -- when would he restore its ancient property?
#lem: aŋ[thing]N; ul[distant time]; ki[place]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=E.100

E.101. %e mu-un-gur₁₁-bi %s tum₉-e %e ba-ab-ir-ra-am₃
#tr.en: Its possessions have been carried off by the wind!
#lem: mungur[property]N; tumu[wind]; ir[bring]
#etcsl: line-id=E.101

E.102. %e uru₂ %s ŋal₂-la-bi nu-ŋal₂-la mi-ni-in-kur₉-ra-am₃
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} turned the city which used to be there into a city no longer!
#lem: uru[city]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=E.102

E.103. dim₂-ma-bi ŋiri₃ ib₂-ta-an-kur₂-ra-am₃
#tr.en: He made its mind wander!
#lem: dimma[thought]; ŋiri[foot]; kur[different]
#etcsl: line-id=E.103

E.104. umuš-bi in-suh₃-am₃ lil₂-e bi₂-in-sag₃-ga-am₃
#tr.en: He threw its intelligence into disorder and made it haunted!
#lem: umuš[consideration]; suh[confuse]; lil[ghost]; sag[strike]
#etcsl: line-id=E.104

E.105. u₂-bi a-bi ib₂-ta-an-kar-ra-am₃
#tr.en: He took away its food and its water!
#lem: u[plant(s)]; a[water]; kar[flee]
#etcsl: line-id=E.105

E.106. ga zu kaš zu-a ud-bi mi-ni-ib-til-la-am₃
#tr.en: He brought to an end its days of familiarity with milk and with beer!
#lem: ga[milk]; zu[know]; kaš[beer]; zu[know]; ud[sun]; til[complete]
#etcsl: line-id=E.106

E.107. e₂-e %e aŋ₂-gig %s bi₂-ib-ak-a
#tr.en: The temple which he has made a sacrilege utters bitter lamentations;
#lem: e[house]; aŋgig[bad thing]N; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=E.107

E.108. %e a-še-er %s gig im-me er₂ bi₂-ib-lu₃-lu₃
#tr.en: he has made its eyes blurred with tears.
#lem: ašer[lament]N; gig[sick]; dug[speak]; er[tears]; lu[mix]
#etcsl: line-id=E.108

E.109. balaŋ di lu₂ i-lu ba-ab-be₂-a
#tr.en: The lamenters who perform the dirges respond to it sorrowfully.
#lem: balaŋ[an instrument]; di[speak]; lu[person]; ilu[lament]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=E.109

E.110. šag₄ %e nu-ze₂-ba-bi %s mu-na-ni-ib-gi₄-gi₄
#tr.en: No one touches the arm of the city's
