R.280. kug-kug-ga šub-ba šu pel₂-la₂-a-ke₄ ki-bi-še₃ in-ŋar-ra
#tr.en: he has put back in their place the most sacred things, neglected and defiled.
#lem: kug[pure]; šub[fall]; šu[hand]; pel[defile]; ki[place]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=R.280

R.281. šukur₂-ud šub-ba eša zid₂ dub-dub-bu %e na-aŋ₂-še₃ %s bi₂-ib-tar-re
#tr.en: He decrees as a fate the offering of daily rations and the grinding up of fine meal and flour.
#lem: šukurud[daily ration]; šub[fall]; eša[fine flour]; zid[flour]; dub[heap up]; naŋ[fate]N; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=R.281

R.282. {ŋiš}banšur ninda lu ninda šar₂-re-da šag₄-ga-ni im-de₆-a
#tr.en: He has decided to make bread plentiful on the table, to make loaves numerous!
#lem: banšur[table]; ninda[bread]; lu[abundant]; ninda[bread]; šar[numerous]V/i; šag[heart]; de[carry]
#etcsl: line-id=R.282

