@div kirugu S

S.284. ud lu₂-u₃ lu₂-ra inim kur₂ nu-di dumu a-a-ni-ir ni₂ teŋ₃-ŋe₂₆-e
#tr.en: Father @wDN{Enlil}, the lord whose command cannot be altered, prince of all countries, has fixed among the black-headed people,
#lem: ud[sun]; lu[person]; lu[person]; inim[word]; kur[alienate]; di[speak]; dumu[child]; aya[father]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]
#etcsl: line-id=S.284

S.285. ud niŋ₂-sun₅-na kalam-ma ŋa₂-ŋa₂ tur-re mah dugud-da
#tr.en: and commanded for their benefit, a time when no one is to speak hostile words to another,
#lem: ud[sun]; niŋsun[humility]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; ŋar[put]; tur[small]; mah[great]; dugud[heavy]
#etcsl: line-id=S.285

S.286. ud šeš-ban₃-da šeš-gal-la-ni hu#-luh-ha ni₂ sun₅-e
#tr.en: when a son is to respect his father, a time to establish humility in the Land,
#lem: ud[sun]; šešbanda[kinship term]; šešgal[kinship term]; huluh[frightened]; ni[self]; sun[humble]
#etcsl: line-id=S.286

S.287. [ud] dumu# gal-la dumu ban₃-da umun₂ ak inim-ma-ni-še₃ tuš-u₃
#tr.en: for the inferior to be as important as the mighty, a time when the younger brother,
#lem: ud[sun]; dumu[child]; gal[big]; dumu[child]; banda[junior]; umun[knowledge]; ak[do]; inim[word]; tuš[sit (down)]
#etcsl: line-id=S.287

S.288. [ud] sig₉-ga kalag-ga še₂₉-eš₂ nu-di niŋ₂ sag₉-ga gal gub-bu
#tr.en: fearing his big brother, is to show humility,
#lem: ud[sun]; sig[weak]; kalag[strong]; heše[oppressed]; di[speak]; niŋ[thing]; sag[good]; gal[big]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=S.288

S.289. [ud] kaskal# suh₃-a ŋiri₃ ŋa₂-ŋa₂ hul mu₂-a bur₁₂-re
#tr.en: a time when the elder child is to treat the younger child reasonably and to pay heed to his words,
#lem: ud[sun]; kaskal[way]; suh[confuse]; ŋiri[foot]; ŋar[put]; hulu[bad]; mu[grow]; bur[tear out]
#etcsl: line-id=S.289

@variants

S.290. [ud lu₂]-u₃ ki šag₄-ga-ni-še₃ du-u₃ gaba-ri-ni-še₃ in nu-dub₂
#tr.en: a time to take neither weak nor strong away into captivity, but to serve with great acts of good,
#lem: ud[sun]; lu[person]; ki[place]; šag[heart]; du[go]; gabari[equal]; in[abuse]; dub[tremble]
#etcsl: line-id=S.290

@variant

#etcsl#ms 1 ms. has instead the line:
S.290A. [ud lu₂]-u₃ ki šag₄-ga-ni-še₃ du-u₃ edin#-na ni₂ sun₅-ni niŋ₂-gig-ga nu-ak
?#tr.en: a time to travel the disordered roadways, to extirpate evil growths, @varh[t224.v6]{a time when anyone is to go where they will,
?#tr.en: to hurl no insults at one's fellow, } @vart[t224.v7,t224.v6]{@varn{1 ms. has instead the line:} a time when anyone is to go where they will, to carry oneself humbly in the plain, to perform no sacrilege, } @varh[t224.v8]{a time no one is to speak hostile words to another,
?#tr.en: to perform no sacrilege, } @vart[t224.v9,t224.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead the line:} a time to go from one's own city to a foreign city, to have no fear on the plain, to perform no sacrilege, } a time to remove bitterness from the Land,
?#tr.en: to establish light therein,
?#tr.en: a time when darkness is to be lifted in the Land, so that living things should rejoice.
#lem: ud[sun]; lu[person]; ki[place]; šag[heart]; du[go]; eden[back]; ni[self]; sun[humble]; niŋgig[that which is bad]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=S.290A

@endvariants
@variants

