@div kirugu T

T.297. i₃-ne-eš₂ a₂-še ud-da-ta {d}en-lil₂ nun šag₄-la₂ sug₄-ga-am₃
#tr.en: Now, see!
#lem: ineš[now]; aše[now]; udata[hereafter]; Enlil[1]DN; nun[prince]; šala[pity]; sug[full]
#etcsl: line-id=T.297

T.298. šul šeg₁₂ TU-ra ŋar-ra-ni-ir in-na-an-sag₉-am₃
#tr.en: After that time, @wDN{Enlil},
#lem: šul[youth]; šeg[brick]; X; ŋar[put]; sag[good]
#etcsl: line-id=T.298

T.299. me erim₂-e šu hul bi₂-in-dug₄-ga si in-na-an-sa₂-am₃
#tr.en: the prince who is full of pity, has been beneficent to his hero who had laid the …… brick!
#lem: me[Being]; erim[enemy]; šu[hand]; hulu[bad]; dug[speak]; si[horn]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=T.299

T.300. ŋarza šu pel₂#-la₂ mu-un-na-an-kug-kug-ga-am₃
#tr.en: He put in order again for him the divine powers which had been desecrated by the enemy! He sanctified again the defiled rites for him!
#lem: ŋarza[rites]; šu[hand]; pel[defile]; kug[purify]
#etcsl: line-id=T.300

T.301. gi-gun₄-bi mu-na-an-sikil-am₃ dalla mu-un-na-an-e₃-am₃
#tr.en: He purified its ziggurat temple and made it resplendent for him! Within he made abundance plentiful,
#lem: giguna[high sacred terrace]; sikil[pure]; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=T.301

T.302. šag₄-ba he₂-ŋal₂ mi-ni-in-šar₂-šar₂-ra-am₃ kurun lal₃ bi₂-ib-si-am₃
#tr.en: he filled it with choice beer and syrup! He established there at that time the pleasing of hearts,
#lem: šag[heart]; heŋal[plenty]; šar[numerous]V/i; kurun[beer]; lal[syrup]; si[fill]
#etcsl: line-id=T.302

T.303. ud ne šag₄ dug₃-ge bar huŋ-e ur₅ sag₉-ge mi-ni-in-ŋar-ra-am₃
#tr.en: the appeasing of spirits, the ameliorating of moods!
#lem: ud[sun]; nen[this]; šag[heart]; dug[good]; bar[outside]; huŋ[pacify]; ur[liver]; sag[good]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=T.303

T.304. e-ne a-ra-zu-a mu-na-an-gub-ba-am₃ giri₁₇ šu mi-ni-ŋal₂-la-am₃
#tr.en: @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}} himself stood in prayer to @wDN{Enlil} and offered salutations!
#lem: ane[he]; arazu[supplication]; gub[stand]; kiri[nose]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=T.304

T.305. er₂ ŋar-ra nam-šita dug₄-ga-ni nun kur-kur-ra-ke₄
#tr.en: When he had begun the lament and spoken the supplication,
#lem: er[tears]; ŋar[put]; namšita[prayer]; dug[speak]; nun[prince]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=T.305

T.306. i₃-he-nun-na lal₃ ku₇-ku₇-da-gin₇ su-ni bi₂-ib₂-ak-am₃
#tr.en: the prince of all countries treated his body with oil of abundance as if it were the sweetest syrup!
#lem: ihenunak[precious oil]; lal[syrup]; kud[sweet]; su[flesh]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=T.306

T.307. šudu₃-da-ni ŋiš ba-an-tuku-am₃ igi in-ši-in-bar-ra-am₃
